# Append-only ledgers: concurrent branches both append at EOF, which a textual merge
# reports as a conflict. Union merge keeps both sides' lines; row identity is
# (name, started) / id, never line position, so order does not matter.
runs/experiments.jsonl merge=union
runs/score_matrix.jsonl merge=union
runs/tasks.jsonl merge=union
runs/retro.jsonl merge=union
runs/review.jsonl merge=union
runs/milestones.jsonl merge=union
runs/board.jsonl merge=union
runs/ledger_resolutions.jsonl merge=union
runs/friction.jsonl merge=union
# The memory-arm diagnostics ledger (readouts 4 and 5 of memory_layers_0905). Append-only by
# its own schema, so union is correct for the same reason as the rest.
# ADDED 2026-09-05, after the file had existed for a day with no transport in EITHER direction:
# it was absent from ledger_audit.KEYS, which is what pod_pull_ledgers derives its file list from,
# and pod_push.sh excludes runs/ -- so the 25 rows behind three stopped arms lived only on the
# pod. Missing here it also failed the pre-commit behind-main exemption, which reads this file,
# so rescuing it needed the deliberate-exception flag.
# ROW IDENTITY IS (name, step, ts), NOT (name, step) as this comment first said. An arm relaunched
# under the same name restarts at step 10 and re-visits every step the previous run wrote, and
# b0_mem_m1 was relaunched on 2026-09-05 (19:41 -> 22:35). Measured on the 25 real rows plus that
# relaunch's first three diag steps: (name, step) collides 3 ways -- ('m1', 10) holding
# pool_touched_frac 0.6516 and 0.3258, two different measurements under one key -- while
# (name, step, ts) gives 28 distinct over 28 rows. On the real 25 alone both read 25/25, which is
# why the cheaper key looks right until an arm is relaunched. The ledger carries no run id, so ts
# is the only field separating two runs of one arm. The KEYS entry now exists (ledger_audit.py).
runs/memory_diag.jsonl merge=union

# The MoE-arm diagnostics ledger (readout 4 of moe_0905). Union for the same reason as the rest:
# concurrent branches both append at EOF, and row identity is a key, never line position.
#
# LANDED WITH ITS WRITER, IN ONE COMMIT, and that is the whole lesson of the block above: the
# memory ledger had a writer for a full DAY with no transport in either direction, so 25 rows
# behind three stopped arms lived only on the pod and rescuing them needed the deliberate-exception
# flag. Three registrations, not one -- this line, the data/ledger_schema.json entry, and the
# scripts/ledger_audit.py KEYS entry, which is what pod_pull_ledgers derives its file list from.
#
# ROW IDENTITY IS (name, step, ts). A MoE arm relaunched after a stop rule fires restarts at step
# 10 and re-visits every step the previous run wrote, and a relaunch is the EXPECTED case here
# rather than a contingency -- measured on the memory ledger, where (name, step) collided three
# ways on b0_mem_m1's relaunch while (name, step, ts) gave 28 distinct over 28 rows.
runs/moe_diag.jsonl merge=union

# EXPERIMENTS.md is DERIVED (exp.py render from runs/experiments.jsonl), so "pick a side" is
# never the right resolution: the driver regenerates it. MEASURED 2026-09-04 that it needs
# one -- two branches each adding a row and rendering produce a real
# `CONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in EXPERIMENTS.md`, because render inserts newest-first
# and both sides write the same top lines. Its source merges by union and does not conflict.
#
# THE COMMAND IS NOT HERE. `git config merge.aupai-experiments.driver` holds it, per clone
# and untracked: this line alone gives a merge that cannot find its driver, the same shape as
# a hook edited in a branch worktree. `harness install-hooks` writes the config;
# `python3 scripts/merge_drivers.py --check` says whether both halves are present here.
# data/pod_head_manifest.txt had a driver and it is REMOVED: the file is untracked now, and
# the driver never fired for it anyway. A merge driver only runs on a CONFLICT, and two
# branches touching different manifest lines merge cleanly -- git spliced one side's line
# with the other side's file content at 81f091af, so main asserted a hash for a file it did
# not contain, with the driver configured and attributed the whole time.
EXPERIMENTS.md merge=aupai-experiments
